    ("I'm sure it wasn't Tom you saw at the station; he's in Berlin.", "BEEN", "It ______________________________ Tom you saw at the station; he's in Berlin.", ["cannot have been", "couldn't have been", "can't have been", "could not have been"], "Záporná jistota v minulosti: 'cannot have been' / 'couldn't have been'.", "V britské angličtině se nepoužívá 'mustn't have been'!"),
